From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 22:49:20 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 06/13] power: supply: iceland-supervooc: no CPU idle exit
 latency during a session

Request a CPU latency of 0 instead of 400 us while a session runs. jstockdale saw
two silent resets with deep idle allowed during a SuperVOOC session; the frame
timing rules (1.5 ms per reply) also favour no idle exit latency.

Based on dappermint/iceland-supervooc commit 614469fabe59 ("ci: run the host tests on every push");
builds on DocZ13's SC8547D handover in iceland-linux issue #2 and on OnePlus's open-source oplus_chg code.

Link: https://github.com/dappermint/iceland-supervooc

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/power/supply/iceland-supervooc/iceland_supervooc.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/power/supply/iceland-supervooc/iceland_supervooc.c b/drivers/power/supply/iceland-supervooc/iceland_supervooc.c
index b32738de6f816..2938c945c85d4 100644
--- a/drivers/power/supply/iceland-supervooc/iceland_supervooc.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/iceland-supervooc/iceland_supervooc.c
@@ -1168,7 +1168,8 @@ static void session(void)
 	pm_runtime_get_sync(busdev);	/* the first frame comes 0.5 s after the last transfer, past geni's 250 ms autosuspend */
 	if (busdev2)
 		pm_runtime_get_sync(busdev2);
-	cpu_latency_qos_add_request(&S.qos, 400);
+	/* iceland: no CPU idle exit latency at all during a session (dappermint: 400 us); jstockdale saw silent resets */
+	cpu_latency_qos_add_request(&S.qos, 0);
 	S.qos_on = true;
 	S.t0 = ktime_get();
 	S.bat_ok = S.t0;
-- 
